      <!-- AGENT MODE -->
      <section id="agent-mode" class="mb-20">
        <h2 id="agent-mode-heading" class="font-display font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Agent Mode</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-light mb-6">
          Hand your bot a card or a slug and let it ship. With Agent Mode, an assistant like Grok Bot runs plan, build,
          review and release on its own. It asks only what matters, all at once, and you approve the PR.
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <div>
            <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Turn it on</p>
            <div class="space-y-2">
              <CommandLine command="npx codeadd install --providers claude --enable-feature agent-mode" />
              <p class="text-muted text-xs">Already using codeadd? Run <code class="font-mono">npx codeadd modify --providers claude --force --enable-feature agent-mode</code>.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-3">How it works</p>
            <ol class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
              <li class="bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
                <p class="text-accent font-mono text-xs mb-1">1</p>
                <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-1">You talk to your bot</p>
                <p class="text-muted-light text-sm">Point it at a card, a slug or a one-line idea.</p>
              </li>
              <li class="bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
                <p class="text-accent font-mono text-xs mb-1">2</p>
                <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-1">The bot runs codeadd</p>
                <p class="text-muted-light text-sm">Plan, build, review and done, one command after the other.</p>
              </li>
              <li class="bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
                <p class="text-accent font-mono text-xs mb-1">3</p>
                <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-1">You answer once</p>
                <p class="text-muted-light text-sm">Open questions come together, each with a recommendation.</p>
              </li>
              <li class="bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/10 rounded-lg p-4">
                <p class="text-accent font-mono text-xs mb-1">4</p>
                <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-1">You approve the PR</p>
                <p class="text-muted-light text-sm">The bot merges on green CI and can cut the release.</p>
              </li>
            </ol>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-2">Why it is easy</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-muted-light text-sm">
              <li><strong class="text-foreground">No interactive stops.</strong> Commands never wait on a menu or a yes/no to continue.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-foreground">Questions batched.</strong> Everything a step needs arrives in one numbered message. Reply <code class="font-mono text-xs">recommended</code> to accept them all.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-foreground">Clear status at the end.</strong> Every run ends as done, stopped, needs-approval or failed, with the reason and the next command.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-foreground">Parallel agents, isolated.</strong> Each agent works in its own git worktree and its own session, so three or four can run side by side.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div>
            <p class="text-foreground text-sm font-semibold mb-2">What you tell the bot</p>
            <blockquote class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-4 text-foreground text-sm italic">Take the dark-mode-toggle card, build it and open the PR for me.</blockquote>
          </div>

          <p class="text-muted text-xs">Works on Claude Code, Cursor and OpenCode. Building your own bot? The technical guide (headless calls, sessions and the result schema) is installed at <a href="https://github.com/brabos-ai/code-addiction/blob/main/framwork/.codeadd/agent-mode/README.md" class="font-mono text-accent hover:underline">.codeadd/agent-mode/README.md</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- PLUGINS -->
      <section id="plugins" class="mb-20">
        <h2 id="plugins-heading" class="font-display font-bold text-2xl sm:text-3xl mb-4">Plugins</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-light mb-6">
          Plugins integrate external tools (MCP servers or skills you install) into ADD commands. Code Addiction handles utilization —
          it validates the tool is present, injects guidance into commands and agents, and activates
          plugin-bound skills. Plugins are <strong>disabled by default</strong> and require the
          external tool to be installed first.
        </p>

        <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-8">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-white/5 bg-white/[0.02] hover:border-accent/20 transition-colors">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="text-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold">gitnexus</code>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted border border-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">mcp</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted-light text-sm mb-2">The agents see who calls what before they change code, so they miss fewer side effects.</p>
            <p class="text-muted text-xs">Used by: <code class="font-mono">add-new</code>, <code class="font-mono">add-plan</code>, <code class="font-mono">add-build</code>, <code class="font-mono">add-diagnose</code>, <code class="font-mono">add-hotfix</code>, <code class="font-mono">add-done</code>, <code class="font-mono">add-wiki</code></p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-white/5 bg-white/[0.02] hover:border-accent/20 transition-colors">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="text-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold">playwright</code>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted border border-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">mcp</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted-light text-sm mb-2">The QA review drives the browser live (screenshots, console, network) instead of reading saved images.</p>
            <p class="text-muted text-xs">Used by: <code class="font-mono">add-review</code></p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-white/5 bg-white/[0.02] hover:border-accent/20 transition-colors">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
              <code class="text-accent font-mono text-sm font-bold">design</code>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted border border-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">skill</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted-light text-sm mb-2">UI plans get a style, palette and type choice from a design library instead of defaults.</p>
            <p class="text-muted text-xs">Used by: <code class="font-mono">add-plan</code></p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-muted text-xs mb-8">Not sure which to enable? <a href="#setup" class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-dim">/add-setup</a> offers each one with a recommendation for your project.</p>

        <!-- gitnexus -->
        <div class="border border-white/5 rounded-xl p-6 bg-white/[0.02] space-y-6">

          <!-- Header -->
          <div>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-2">
              <code class="text-accent font-mono text-lg font-bold">gitnexus</code>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted border border-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">disabled by default</span>
              <span class="text-xs text-muted border border-white/10 px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">mcp</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-muted-light text-sm mb-1">Code knowledge-graph navigation (call graph, refs, blast-radius) via MCP. Enables structural code navigation across discovery, planning, diagnosis, and hotfix commands — going beyond grep to understand actual call chains and impact.</p>
